From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: add inert TC-offload
 block registration

Continuation of the PPE hardware flow-offload port -- see
project_flint3_ppe_hw_offload_research.md for the full architectural
context. This is the first half of the TC-hook shim, split
deliberately in two per prior review: this half only registers the TC
block callback so the kernel's flow-offload infrastructure can find
this driver and offer it flows; ppe_offload_flow_cmd() declines every
FLOW_CLS_REPLACE with -EOPNOTSUPP rather than parsing a flow_rule or
programming any hardware. The second half -- actually accepting and
programming flows -- is a separate, larger change that needs its own
review and the project's live-hardware go-ahead, not bundled in here.

Modeled on drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe_offload.c's TC block
bind/unbind handling (flow_block_cb_alloc/_lookup/_incref/_decref/
_add/_remove, requiring FLOW_BLOCK_BINDER_TYPE_CLSACT_INGRESS), read
in full before writing this. Only one PPE instance exists per SoC, so
a single file-scope block callback list is sufficient rather than
introducing a per-device context struct now -- the hardware-programming
half will need real state (an rhashtable of offloaded flows, links to
the host/nexthop pools from 0418) and is expected to introduce that
struct when it lands, not before.

Wires .ndo_setup_tc onto edma_port_netdev_ops, which -- unlike 0419's
register write -- has no runtime effect on its own: NETIF_F_HW_TC is
deliberately *not* set on the netdevice's features in this patch, and
this project's current nftables config uses software flowtables
(kmod-nft-offload) with no hardware-offload flag, so nothing in the
kernel's flow-offload infrastructure has any reason to call this
callback in the current running configuration. It is reachable only if
something explicitly requests hardware-offloaded TC/nftables flow
acceleration on one of these netdevices, which nothing does yet.

Compile-tested only (module builds and links cleanly, all three new
symbols present); no hardware testing has been done.

Signed-off-by: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/Makefile
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
